<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Lausanne</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1923">1923</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkish-war-of-independence">Turkish War of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lausanne">Lausanne</a>, signed on 24 July 1923, settled the conflict between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> and the Turkish nationalist government, replacing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-sevres">Treaty of Sèvres</a>. It recognised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>'s borders in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>, including Smyrna, confirmed Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over most <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> islands and Italian possession of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dodecanese">Dodecanese</a>, and accompanied the Greek–Turkish population exchange.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-lausanne.jpg" alt="Treaty of Lausanne" width="320" height="164" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Turkey-Greece-Bulgaria_on_Treaty_of_Lausanne.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
